notes               = "One poem running across two printed pages: the dedication and the opening are on 184, the date and a printed footnote on 185. The dedication با یاد مادرم «مَلَک» ('in memory of my mother, Malak' — ملک is Angel) is printed in the outer margin. An elegy for the poet's mother, matching the father poems on 146-147. THE POEM IS BUILT ON A NAME IT DOES NOT DISCLOSE UNTIL THE FOOTNOTE: عاطفه means tenderness or affection, and only under the rule on page 185 does the asterisk reveal that Atefeh is also the name of his mother's nurse — the same device as turquoise-mirror (174), where فیروزه is both turquoise and the dedicatee. The printed footnote has been moved out of the body into ===footnotes===. Last line of 184, دیشب تبی نیامده... تابش برد: تاب بردن is to carry off someone's strength, so a fever that had not properly arrived took her; the line is compressed and the reading is not certain. 26 Ordibehesht = 16 May 2001. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

تا یاد دارمش...
در هاله‌ای از عاطفه می‌لغزید.
بر گونه‌های مادر...
از برگ‌های عاطفه باغی بود...
از رنگ‌های عاطفه گلزاری...
مویش سیاه بود... و
سال‌های بعد... دودی شد...
از دود بید و شاخهٔ انگور...
در شعله‌ها
و ساقه‌های گندم و خشخاش...
که شعله می‌شدند... در زیر دیگ آش.
همیشه چشم‌هاش... پُر بود از نگاهی امیدوار...
و در متن انتظارش...
موسیقی دعا جریان داشت...
و سطح ندبه‌اش... دیوار مطبخی...
که از سیاهی برق می‌زد.
با یادِ مادر... من هرچه نذر کردم... شد...
و هرچه کاشتم رویید... و...
گل کرد و میوه داد.
بر گونه‌های مادر...
از برگ‌های عاطفه باغی بود...
از رنگ‌های عاطفه گلزاری...
دیشب تبی نیامده... تابش برد....
مادر به راه این سفرِ جاوید...
بربال‌های عاطفه* خوابش برد...
۱۳۸۰/۲/۲۶

===machine===

For as long as I can remember her...
she moved in a halo of tenderness.
On my mother's cheeks...
there was a garden made of the leaves of tenderness...
a flower-bed made of the colours of tenderness...
Her hair was black... and
in the years after... it turned smoke-coloured...
from the smoke of willow and vine-branch...
in the flames,
and the stalks of wheat and poppy...
that became flame... under the soup pot.
Her eyes were always... full of a hopeful looking...
and through the whole text of her waiting...
the music of prayer was running...
and the surface of her lamenting... a kitchen wall...
that shone black with soot.
Remembering my mother... whatever I vowed... came about...
and whatever I planted grew... and...
flowered and bore fruit.
On my mother's cheeks...
there was a garden made of the leaves of tenderness...
a flower-bed made of the colours of tenderness...
Last night a fever that had not even arrived... carried her strength away....
Mother, on the road of this everlasting journey...
fell asleep on the wings of Atefeh*...
1380/2/26

===lantern===

For as long as I can remember her
she moved in a halo of tenderness.
On my mother's cheeks
there was a garden made of the leaves of tenderness,
a flower-bed made of the colours of tenderness.
Her hair was black, and
in the years after it turned the colour of smoke —
smoke of willow and vine-branch
in the flames,
and stalks of wheat and poppy
that became flame under the soup pot.
Her eyes were always full of a hopeful looking,
and through the whole text of her waiting
the music of prayer was running,
and the surface of her lamenting was a kitchen wall
that shone black with soot.
Remembering my mother: whatever I vowed came about,
and whatever I planted grew,
and flowered, and bore fruit.
On my mother's cheeks
there was a garden made of the leaves of tenderness,
a flower-bed made of the colours of tenderness.
Last night a fever that had not even arrived carried her strength away.
Mother, on the road of this everlasting journey,
fell asleep on the wings of Atefeh...

1380/2/26

===translation===

===footnotes===

عاطفه — *Atefeh* — is the word for tenderness, affection, the thing the whole poem has been
describing on the mother's face. The printed page carries an asterisk on its last use of the word
and answers it beneath the frame:

> عاطفه نام پرستار مهربان مادر — *Atefeh is the name of mother's kind nurse.*

So the last line means both that she fell asleep on the wings of tenderness and that she died in the
arms of a woman called Tenderness, and the poem does not tell you until it is over. English can keep
the name or the meaning, not both at once.
